WEBVTT

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.910
What's got you in such a rush?

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:14.770
Lupin!

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.880
I'm guessing the idea of someone 
else stealing your score

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.740
got you so anxious that you just 
<i>had</i> to do something, right?

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.580
Maybe you're still a thief, after all.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.850
Didn't I explain it to you already?

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:31.580
I only became a cop so I could 
go after a much bigger target.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.580
And what brings you here?

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.740
Who, me? Just thought I'd ask 
our mutual friend here

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.160
about the pests that have been 
swarming around me lately.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.970
Then, our interests align nicely.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.850
I'll leave the interrogation to you.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.990
You've got a knack for getting bad 
guys to spill their guts, right?

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.160
Albert! What do you think you're doing?!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.830
Do you honestly think you'll get away with—

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.660
I'm the one asking the questions here!

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.980
It was José! He betrayed me!

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.940
He's working behind the scenes for Calvess!

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.740
He's carrying out terrorist attacks to 
help that bastard win the election!

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.220
As long as José has the black notebook,

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.070
the top brass of the police 
will do whatever he wants!

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.230
Th-That goes for me, too!

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.520
José threatened me! I had no choice—

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.810
Where's José now?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.820
He's at the Château de Pouvier!

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.210
There's a castle in its grounds 
that he's using as a hideout!

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.110
What happened to leaving 
the interrogation to me?

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.770
You were pussyfooting around. 
I just wanted to speed things up.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.990
<b>Thief and Thief</b>

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:50.200
It's been a while since 
I gave you a lift anywhere.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.460
Wasn't the last time that job
you screwed up in Helsinki?

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:59.370
Yeah, right. The last time was 
when I saved your butt in Mexico.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.080
Don't be stupid. Nothing like that ever...

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.710
Well? Remember it now?

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:22.750
No. Not at all.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:26.230
You little liar! It's written all over your—

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:33.120
Bulletproof glass: for when 
you'd rather be safe than sorry.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:36.010
Probably contractors working for the DGSE.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.610
You mean, José the Jerk's lackeys?

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:41.350
No, their M.O. is different. 
Guillaume probably sent them.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.330
Their Rolodex of thugs who do 
their dirty work must be huge.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.290
I'm flooring it.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.060
I presume that's your 
knight in shining armor?

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.480
Imagine the look on a princess's face 
if her Prince Charming had that beard...

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.180
Dammit, I missed!

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.960
I'll take care of these guys.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.310
You tag along with Lupin.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.730
I get the feeling it's only gonna 
get worse from here on out.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:33.550
Understood!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.780
Your thief buddies like sticking 
their noses into your business.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.210
Yeah. Funny how you don't have any.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:55.670
Goemon!

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.160
Lupin, I shall deal with this.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:10.460
Oh, you're just my type, honey.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:13.430
I can smell the blood on you!

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.200
Wow, that's a <i>lot</i> of infrared tripwires.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.540
Now, how are we going to sneak in?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.700
Why are you even stopping to think about it? 
Through the front door, of course.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.190
Whoa, hold your horses. They'll see us 
coming from a mile away if we do that.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.090
That girl with the claws was 
lying in wait to ambush us.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.570
They already know we're here.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:47.430
It's a waste of time trying to sneak in.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.230
Have you no sense of panache? 
No flair for being furtive?!

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:55.680
No. I left all that behind 
with you on the bridge.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:01.780
Gotcha. As soon as you 
find them, kill them both.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.180
Damn you, Chlo. You screwed up...

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.760
Or maybe you're up to your old tricks again.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.040
Very nice. I'm positively throbbing.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:40.100
Out of breath already?

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.410
Just nursing the gunshot wound <i>you</i> gave me!

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:45.750
Hasn't that healed yet? 
Old age catching up with you?

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:46.740
Why, you...

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.800
We're gonna have to make a run for it.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:52.840
Okay. On two.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:53.780
Gotcha.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.480
One, <i>two!</i>

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.760
You son of a bitch! You used me as a decoy!

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.640
And it worked perfectly.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.070
That's not the issue!

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:31.500
Hey, how about you be the decoy this time?

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:35.050
Are you stupid? If I jump in there, 
I'll look like Swiss cheese.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.150
That didn't stop you from 
making me run the gauntlet!

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.160
That's because I knew you'd make it through.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.270
Flattery's not getting you anywhere.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.490
It's getting me inside.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.440
<i>Boss! It's Lupin and Albert! 
They're heading your way!</i>

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.330
I see.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:07.680
I have to wonder, though... 
How do they know where I am in the castle?

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.700
<i>Someone must've spilled 
the beans. Am I wrong?</i>

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.390
H-Hold up a sec! I didn't have a choice!

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.230
Go on ahead.

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:40.240
I've got a bone to pick with this one.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.930
Well done.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.530
You're everything I hoped for.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:18.300
But it's time to wrap this up!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:33.540
Most people hang onto their weapon, 
and that's when I nail them...

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.640
You really are something else!

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:39.480
Oh, man, I think I might have the hots for you.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:22.470
I didn't think... you'd use 
the nails you cut off...

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:28.050
I'm just sad I couldn't chew your throat out...

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.400
I figured I might run into you again...

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:53.220
So I brought a little something with me.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.550
Aren't you gonna play along even a little?!

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.240
Gramps...

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:20.670
Consider yourself avenged.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.800
That won't work.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:42.120
There isn't a knife around that 
can cut one of my wires.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.810
Wire cutters made from
a special steel alloy.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.840
Every good thief has a pair.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.130
Really?

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.790
Looks like your arm's busted, though.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:11.530
I don't really like loud toys like this.

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:17.800
But I may as well kill you 
with your own weapon.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.570
I bet that'll be much more 
frustrating, won't it?

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:24.670
I appreciate the extra effort.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:35.870
What is it, Araignée?

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.930
<i>I took care of the intruder, boss.</i>

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:41.490
What a good kid. Well done.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:45.060
That just leaves Lupin.

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:52.440
I guess Revenant screwed up.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.540
Are you here to kill me?

00:14:56.890 --> 00:15:00.200
I remember you trying to kill me first.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.360
And that's game over.

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:25.280
Yeah...

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.570
But I'm the winner.

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:48.160
You're still able to move?

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:53.240
Looks like I need to give 
you another taste of my—

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.480
Now, we're even for Mexico.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.340
Albert...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.590
But how?!

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.760
I've got a knack for imitating voices.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:23.810
That "good kid" of yours 
will be waiting for you in Hell.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:42.630
That was close... Sheesh.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:47.830
He almost took us with him 
on his journey downwards.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.900
Now, I just need to decide 
what to do with this...

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:57.040
Huh? You... When did you...

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:01.500
Looks like he liked to keep 
his valuables on him.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:07.030
Oh! That's when you took it!

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:11.790
Let me have it! You can't 
possibly have a use for it.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.770
Yeah, you've got a point.

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:16.870
Thing is, though, when 
someone wants something,

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.270
I get this overwhelming 
urge to run off with it.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:36.540
Man, you're a thief to the bone, you know that?

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:02.170
Pull over here.

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:21.050
Keep the car. Consider it a parting gift.

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:30.180
Whoa, man, hang in there.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.790
You sure you don't want 
a ride to your place?

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:37.480
Don't. You showing compassion is 
the sort of thing that gives me hives.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.400
Suit yourself.

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:49.480
Albert...

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.810
Looks like you're a thief to the bone, too.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:35.330
You got me.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:39.720
This round goes to you, Lupin III.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:37.640
"Calvess unexpectedly withdraws
from presidential race,"

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:40.820
and "Director General of DGSE arrested."

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:46.000
The media's gonna have plenty of 
material for the foreseeable future.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:50.630
By the way, Lupin, what did 
you do with that black notebook?

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.400
Oh, that thing?

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:55.150
I returned it to its true owner.

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:18.370
Daisuke Jigen here.

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:21.550
We're looking to relieve Pablo, 
a drug kingpin, of his fortune,

00:22:21.550 --> 00:22:23.490
so we're off to South America.

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:27.600
Looks like Pablo keeps his bizarre 
collection out in the jungle.

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:31.320
Didn't think the military would 
be gunning for his assets, too.

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:34.480
Lupin, you need to ditch Fujiko.

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:38.040
If that woman gets her claws into you, 
you'll wind up pushing up daisies.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:45.040
<b>Get Pablo's Collection</b>

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:40.730
Next time: Get Pablo's Collection.

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:43.860
Sometimes you're beyond help, pal.
